RAG: Retrieval Augmented Generation
why RAG:
        instead of providing generalized answers it gives answers on data that we provide , based on our data/context.

        like pdf, docs

RAG pipeline: 
     2 phases: 
        1)indexing
        2)Retrieval

1)Indexing phase(index.py)
    Your Data/Documents
    → Chunk into smaller pieces
    → Convert each chunk into vector embeddings using embedding model
    → Store vectors in vector database(pinecone db, chromadb,pgvector)

   
   2) Retrieval phase(chat.py)

    User Query
    → Convert query into embedding using same/similar embedding model
    → Compare query vector with stored vectors
    → Retrieve most relevant chunks
    → Send retrieved chunks + query to LLM
    → LLM generates final answer


    LangChain:
        LangChain is a framework that helps developers build LLM-powered applications by providing components such as document loaders, PDF parsers, text chunking, embeddings integration, vector database connections, prompt templates, memory, retrievers, and workflow chains

        langchain is a library which provide a lot of utility tools which we can use in day to day ai tasks


        Sync-Async Approach:
        The above(index.py & chat.py) is synchronous approach means it  waits untill process is complet.
        Everything happens step by step, one task waits for the previous one to finish.
        One step blocks next step,time consuming.

        Async Approach:
        Multiple users send queries to server
        Server immediately stores requests in a queue
        Worker/processor consumes queued jobs one by one or in parallel
        Worker runs RAG pipeline:
        embed query
        retrieve from vector DB (e.g. Qdrant)
        call LLM
        generate answer
        Store result in DB/cache
        User polls / websocket receives completed response


